{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And I have separated you from the peoples to be Mine.</b> If you are separated from them — then you are Mine; and if not — then you are Nebuchadnezzar's and his companions'. Rabbi Elazar ben Azaryah says: From where do we know that a person should not say, 'My soul loathes pork flesh, I am unable to wear shatnez' — but rather he should say, 'I am able — but what can I do, when my Father in heaven has decreed upon me?' Scripture says: ״וָאַבְדִּיל אֶתְכֶם מִן הָעַמִּים לִהְיוֹת לִי״ — that your separation from them be for My name: separating from transgression and accepting upon himself the yoke of the kingdom of heaven. (Sifra)"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:28.679970910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}